Z||000024||Robert||05-19-2000||07:45 PM||||You know, looking at the bottles of “Fiero” wine, I see a screw on cap.  Now for someone from the San Francisco Bay area, i.e. near Napa Valley, this is a no no….<BR>Speaking as someone who runs a printing company, I look at things from a different angle.  Why not print “Fiero” labels and apply them to a quality wine?  Less shipping and better wine.  Anyone up for providing some quality art?  I can print anything, just can’t draw worth a damn. Maybe some “Indy Estate Chardonnay” or “GT Merlot”<P>I can see a nice Fiero on the label, appropriate background (garage, large estate?), and some verbiage about the merits of the wine.<P>Just some ideas<P>Robert<BR>Yellow (Muscat Canelli?) 87GT Fastback<BR>||||reg||3
